# MCSP Assembler Seed 0.40

Status: Constructive native assembler experiment
Qualification: Under Conditional Experiment
Parent: NATIVE-MACHINE-DESCRIPTION-0.39

## Objective

Establish the first bounded MCSP assembler mechanism:

    MCSP structural machine description -> selected machine encoding

The assembler seed SHALL make its encoding decision from structural commitments rather than from an assembly mnemonic supplied as semantic input.

## Input structure

For this fixture the admitted structure contains:
- operation relation token: 0x01, defined by 0.39 four-row distinction relation;
- width: 64;
- destination realization register token: 0;
- source realization register token: 3;
- operand form: register/register.

Register tokens and concrete encoding remain x86-64 REALIZATION_DEFINED.

## Output

For the admitted fixture the expected x86-64 encoding is:

    48 31 d8

The emitted bytes are output evidence, not MCSP semantic identity.

## Decision rule

The seed accepts only the exact qualified structural tuple supported by 0.40.

Unsupported or mutated tuples SHALL be rejected rather than guessed.

This deliberately narrow admission rule prevents a lookup table from masquerading as a general assembler.

## Execution qualification

The emitted bytes SHALL be placed in executable memory followed by a return instruction supplied by the harness boundary.

The emitted operation SHALL execute over the 0.39 A/B fixture and produce the structurally predicted destination while preserving the declared source role.

## Boundary

NASM may bootstrap the emitter program but SHALL NOT select the target operation encoding.

The target bytes SHALL be written by the MCSP assembler seed at runtime.

0.40 is not a general x86 assembler.
Kernel remains DETERMINATE CONDITION.
